An interviewer may ask:
1. Can a Java Map contain a null key?
2. Can a Java Map contain multiple null values?
3. Which Map implementations allow null keys and values?
4. Why does ConcurrentHashMap not allow null?
5. How does HashMap internally handle a null key?
6. What happens when we insert multiple null keys?
7. How does TreeMap behave with null keys?
Let's understand this from basic concepts to internal implementation.
1. Null support in different Map implementations
This is the most important interview reference table.

Map                 implementation	Null key	Null values
HashMap	                Yes (one)	Yes (multiple)
LinkedHashMap	        Yes (one)	Yes (multiple)
Hashtable	              No	No
ConcurrentHashMap	      No	No
TreeMap (natural ordering)	No	Yes
TreeMap (custom comparator)	If comparator supports null	Yes
WeakHashMap	              Yes (one)	Yes (multiple)
                          Yes (one) | Yes (multiple)

